  {"id":"519ef69c-a78a-4983-b155-e68494986d0f","term":"Balalaika brrr-strum","verdict":"MINOR","suggestions":[{"field":"definition","severity":"Low","issue":"The definition says the strum runs 'across the courses' and related_terms lists 'Course (paired strings),' implying doubled courses. Web-verified via Wikipedia (Balalaika): the standard/traditional prima balalaika, the instrument this brrr-strum technique belongs to, has THREE SINGLE strings (E4-E4-A4); only less-common factory 6-string variants use three double courses. Calling the strings 'courses' is imprecise for the standard instrument a student would encounter.","suggestion":"Change 'across the courses' to 'across the strings,' and consider replacing the 'Course (paired strings)' related term (e.g., with 'Balalaika prima' or 'Folk lute'), or note that doubled courses appear only on some 6-string variants."}]},
